+"""Experiment 5596: does a larger, MTP-capable generator (Qwen3.6-27B-MTP, the official
+unsloth GGUF matching the operator's exact "qwen-3.6-27B" framing) improve tier-3 induction
+quality over the frozen live generator (Qwen3.5-9B-MTP)?
+
+Context: ops/known-issues.md task 13 (2026-07-12, HIGH PRIORITY). Operator question: "are we
+still using qwen-3.5-9B when the leaders are using the larger and newer qwen-3.6-27B and
+Gemma-4-31b models?" Investigation confirmed Kaggle's ARC-AGI-3 accelerator pool includes an
+RTX Pro 6000 (96GB, g4-standard-48, "ARC-AGI-3 exclusive" per docs.arcprize.org) and that forge's
+real, scored, 3rd-place (LB 0.86) kernel-metadata.json explicitly requests
+`machine_shape: NvidiaRtxPro6000` and ran Gemma-4-31B-it -- direct, real-world confirmation a
+larger accelerator + model combination is genuinely usable and scores successfully in this
+competition (see docs/research-notes/arc-kaggle-accelerator-upgrade-2026-06-21.md's 2026-07-13
+update).
+
+CANDIDATE SELECTION (revised mid-task): the FIRST candidate considered, `unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-
+GGUF`, was found via direct GGUF metadata inspection to have NO MTP/self-draft support at all
+(no nextn_predict_layers key) -- any speedup the 9B model gets from MTP would not carry over,
+confounding a clean size-vs-quality comparison. Operator surfaced a better-fitting pair of
+official candidates mid-task: `unsloth/Qwen3.6-27B-MTP-GGUF` and `unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP-
+GGUF` -- genuinely MTP-capable GGUFs at the exact "Qwen3.6-27B-class" size the operator's
+original question named. This experiment uses the dense 27B variant (the more direct match to
+"Qwen3.6-27B"); the 35B MoE variant is a natural follow-on. MTP support is verified empirically
+in TWO steps, not assumed from the repo name alone: (1) does the GGUF metadata declare an MTP
+head (`_candidate_declares_mtp_metadata()`), and (2) does llama.cpp's SELF-draft MTP (which
+loads the SAME file twice, main + draft) actually FIT in available VRAM
+(`_candidate_mtp_self_draft_fits_vram()`) -- found necessary mid-task after a manual launch
+OOM'd (2x a 16.3GB file does not fit a single 24GB RTX 3090 alongside KV cache/overhead). The
+candidate arm runs WITHOUT MTP when step (2) fails, so the experiment measures a real induction-
+quality delta instead of crash-looping on an infeasible self-draft launch.
+
+Both arms are pinned to the SAME hardware tier (GPU 1, one of the dev box's two RTX 3090s, the
+outer loop's own allocated card per CLAUDE.md's GPU-allocation rule) via
+CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU=1 and a fresh, non-default port per arm, avoiding any stale-server
+reuse ambiguity (the established gotcha from feedback_gguf_outer_loop_gpu_pinning.md).
+
+SCOPE (honest, not the task's full ideal): like exp5594, this measures induction QUALITY via the
+existing WorldModelVerifier.heldout_accuracy, not a full actions-to-first-win live-solve sweep. A
+SECOND official candidate named by task 13 (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-MTP, MoE) is a natural follow-on if
+this result is promising; not tested here to keep this pass focused and cheap.
+
+Per the task's own guardrail (mirroring task 7's frozen-stack discipline): this is an OFFLINE DEV
+MEASUREMENT, not a live-stack change. Do NOT flip the frozen live generator based on this
+experiment alone; report the delta and require an explicit operator decision.
+
